<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Segura River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Segura is a river of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, about 325 km long, rising in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-de-segura">Sierra de Segura</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaen">Jaén</a> and flowing through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murcia">Murcia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orihuela">Orihuela</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> at Guardamar. Its valley and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huerta">huertas</a> of Murcia and Orihuela have been irrigated since Islamic times by networks of canals and water-wheels. The river is subject to severe floods and droughts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/segura-river.jpg" alt="Segura River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Rodriguillo assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Murcia_-_Puente_Viejo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
